  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, and it clearly outperforms single-profile (config_001, 0.485) and transformer aggregation (config_003, 0.519). Image-only is very weak (0.208). The only RNA encoder tested so far is PCA n2000, leaving a major uncertainty: does a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi) improve over linear PCA when the profile and aggregation are held at their best-performing settings? Question: config_005 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while keeping multi-profile + avgpool (the winning combination from config_002), isolating the encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a single-variable comparison against our current best, directly tests a fundamental representation choice that could shift the ceiling for all downstream multimodal experiments, and avoids prematurely committing budget to multimodal fusion when the RNA backbone itself may not yet be optimized. If scvi matches or beats PCA, we gain confidence in the encoder direction; if it underperforms, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can pivot to multimodal or scgpt with clearer rationale."
}

